  simulationStarted: "The bus will test the workers' crossing. Consider how the whole bridge carries the required traffic."
  liveLoadStarted: "The bus's weight is reaching the bridge. Follow the load path through the roadway, members, and supports."
  vehicleEnteredBridge: "The bus is entering the bridge. Check that the roadway and supporting members remain connected."
  vehicleReachedMidpoint: "The bus is near the middle. Watch how individual members share the load as its position changes."
  vehicleApproachingEnd: "The bus is approaching the opposite bank. Keep observing until the entire vehicle has crossed."
  highStressDetected: "Some members are using a large share of their capacity. Inspect their supports and the surrounding load path."
  stressLimitExceeded: "The bridge exceeded the contract's stress limit. Review the overloaded area before changing your design."
  firstMemberBreak: "A member failed. Identify where the first problem began and how the remaining members carry the load."
  vehicleStuck: "The bus has stopped moving. Check the road alignment, clearance, and connections."
  vehicleFailed: "The bus could not finish the crossing. Use the results to identify which parts need improvement."
  bridgeSucceeded: "The bus reached the far bank. Your connected bridge carried the required live load through the crossing."
  simulationStopped: "Simulation stopped. Review the results and use your reasoning to guide any changes."
